meta {
  name: Docker Exec (WebSocket)
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/ws/docker/containers/{{container_id}}/exec
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{jwt_token}}
}

docs {
  Interactive container shell over WebSocket. The handler in
  src/routes/ws/docker.rs spawns a `docker exec` and bridges its stdio
  with the socket: client → exec stdin (text/binary frames), exec
  stdout/stderr → client (text frames).

  Bruno itself can't drive WS; use wscat:
    wscat -c "ws://localhost:8080/ws/docker/containers/$CID/exec?cmd=ls" \
      -H "Authorization: Bearer $JWT_TOKEN"

  Query params:
    cmd    — command line to run (default `/bin/sh`). Parsed with
             shell-words, so quoted segments stay intact:
               `cmd=sh -c "echo hi"` → argv ["sh", "-c", "echo hi"]
             An unmatched quote or empty result yields 400 BAD_REQUEST.
    tty    — bool, default false
    stdin  — bool, default true

  Hardening:
    - max_message_size / max_frame_size capped at 64 KiB
    - server-driven 30s ping; closes after 5 min without inbound activity
    - master kill-switch via `docker.exec_enabled` in config (default true);
      when false the upgrade is refused with 503

  Known gap (tracked):
    - No per-token scope check. Any device with a valid access token can
      reach root-equivalent privilege inside any container — flip
      `exec_enabled = false` in production unless interactive shells are
      an explicit, audited workflow.
}
